## 0. The basics (read this first)

> **In plain words, a web page has 3 parts:**  
> 🧱 **HTML** = WHAT is on the page (boxes, buttons, text, images)  
> 🎨 **CSS** = HOW it looks (colors, size, position)  
> ⚙️ **JavaScript** = WHAT HAPPENS when you click, type, or move the mouse

### The skeleton – start EVERY task with this

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="hu">
<head>
  <meta charset="UTF-8">
  <title>Feladat</title>
  <link rel="stylesheet" href="style.css">   <!-- only if you have a style.css file -->
  <style>
    /* OR write CSS here */
  </style>
</head>
<body>

  <!-- HTML (the visible stuff) goes here -->

  <script>
    // JavaScript goes here, AT THE BOTTOM of body
  </script>
</body>
</html>
```

### The 5 golden rules of JavaScript

| \#  | Rule                                                  | Code                                                 |
|-----|-------------------------------------------------------|------------------------------------------------------|
| 1   | Anything JS needs to touch gets an **id**             | `<input id="tipp">`                                  |
| 2   | **READ** what the user typed                          | `document.getElementById("tipp").value`              |
| 3   | **WRITE** text onto the page                          | `document.getElementById("ki").innerHTML = "Hello";` |
| 4   | Inputs always give you TEXT, so turn it into a number | `Number(document.getElementById("tipp").value)`      |
| 5   | A button runs a function                              | `<button onclick="tippel()">Tippel</button>`         |

> 💡 **Shortcut your teacher uses:** if an element has `id="tipp"`, you can just write `tipp.value` instead of `document.getElementById("tipp").value`. Both work. The long version is safer.

> 💡 **Press F12 → Console** in the browser. Red text there = your error and the line number.

## 1. How style.css works

### Connecting style.css to your HTML

Put this line inside `<head>`. The file `style.css` must be in the **same folder** as the .html file.

```html
<link rel="stylesheet" href="style.css">
```

> ⚠️ Inside **style.css** you write ONLY CSS. No `<style>` tags, no HTML.

### How one CSS rule looks

```css
selector {
  property: value;
  property: value;
}

/* example: */
h1 {
  color: red;
  font-size: 30px;
}
```

In plain words: "find these elements, then give them these looks." Every line ends with **;** and the rule is wrapped in **{ }**.

### Selectors – WHO gets styled

| CSS                | Picks                                       | HTML it matches                  |
|--------------------|---------------------------------------------|----------------------------------|
| `p { }`            | every \<p\> tag                             | `<p>Hi</p>`                      |
| `.doboz { }`       | everything with class="doboz" (dot = class) | `<div class="doboz">`            |
| `#ki { }`          | the ONE element with id="ki" (hashtag = id) | `<p id="ki">`                    |
| `.doboz img { }`   | images INSIDE a .doboz                      | `<div class="doboz"><img></div>` |
| `h1, h2 { }`       | both h1 and h2                              |                                  |
| `button:hover { }` | button WHILE the mouse is over it           |                                  |
| `tr:hover td { }`  | cells of the row under the mouse            |                                  |

> 💡 Strength order when rules fight: **\#id** beats **.class**, and **.class** beats **tag**. If two rules are equally strong, the one written LOWER in the file wins.

### The box model – every element is a box

```text
+---------------- margin (space OUTSIDE the border) ----------------+
|   +------------------- border (the line) ---------------------+   |
|   |   +------------ padding (space INSIDE) ---------------+   |   |
|   |   |                                                    |   |   |
|   |   |              CONTENT (width x height)              |   |   |
|   |   |                                                    |   |   |
|   |   +----------------------------------------------------+   |   |
|   +------------------------------------------------------------+   |
+--------------------------------------------------------------------+
```

```css
.doboz {
  width: 400px;              /* how wide */
  height: 300px;             /* how tall */
  padding: 20px;             /* push content away from the edge (inside) */
  border: 2px solid black;   /* thickness  style  color */
  margin: 30px;              /* push OTHER things away (outside) */
  border-radius: 10px;       /* rounded corners */
  box-sizing: border-box;    /* padding + border count INSIDE the width (easier math) */
}

/* margin/padding shortcuts: */
margin: 10px;               /* all 4 sides */
margin: 10px 20px;          /* top+bottom 10, left+right 20 */
margin: 0 auto;             /* top+bottom 0, left+right AUTOMATIC = horizontally centered */
margin-top: 10px;           /* only one side (also -bottom, -left, -right) */
```

### Most important properties

| Property           | What it does                          | Example                                                                                |
|--------------------|---------------------------------------|----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|
| `color`            | text color                            | `color: red;` / `#ff0000` / `rgb(255,0,0)`                                             |
| `background-color` | background color                      | `background-color: lightblue;`                                                         |
| `background-image` | image as background                   | `background-image: url("kep.jpg");`                                                    |
| `font-size`        | text size                             | `font-size: 20px;`                                                                     |
| `font-family`      | font                                  | `font-family: Arial, sans-serif;`                                                      |
| `font-weight`      | bold                                  | `font-weight: bold;`                                                                   |
| `text-align`       | text left/center/right INSIDE its box | `text-align: center;`                                                                  |
| `display`          | how it behaves                        | `block` (own line), `inline` (in the text), `flex` (arrange children), `none` (hidden) |
| `position`         | exact placement                       | `relative` / `absolute` (see section 3)                                                |
| `cursor`           | mouse pointer look                    | `pointer` (hand), `crosshair` (+)                                                      |
| `border-collapse`  | table: single lines instead of double | `border-collapse: collapse;`                                                           |
| `box-shadow`       | shadow                                | `box-shadow: 0 2px 8px gray;`                                                          |

### Units

|             |                                                                    |
|-------------|--------------------------------------------------------------------|
| `px`        | pixels (fixed size). Use this when unsure.                         |
| `%`         | percent of the parent box                                          |
| `vh` / `vw` | percent of the SCREEN height / width. `100vh` = full screen height |

## 2. Put a box in the middle of the screen

> In plain words: make the **body** as tall as the screen, then tell it to **center its children** both ways.

**Full working file**

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="hu">
<head>
<meta charset="UTF-8">
<title>Doboz középen</title>
<style>
  body {
    margin: 0;                  /* remove the default white border around the page */
    height: 100vh;              /* body = full screen height */
    display: flex;              /* turn on "arrange my children" mode */
    justify-content: center;    /* children to the middle LEFT-RIGHT */
    align-items: center;        /* children to the middle UP-DOWN */
    background-color: #dfe6f5;
  }

  .doboz {
    width: 500px;
    height: 300px;
    background-color: white;
    border: 2px solid black;
    border-radius: 10px;
  }
</style>
</head>
<body>

  <div class="doboz">
    I am the box
  </div>

</body>
</html>
```

> 💡 **Only left-right centering** (box stays at the top): forget flex and just give the box `margin: 50px auto;`

> ⚠️ Vertical centering not working? You forgot `height: 100vh;` on body. Without it, body is only as tall as its content, so there is nothing to center in.

## 3. Move content inside the box

### Way A – Center text: `text-align`

```css
.doboz {
  text-align: center;   /* left | center | right   (works on text, inputs, buttons, images) */
}
```

### Way B – Flex (easiest for "put it in the middle / corner")

Put `display: flex` on the **BOX** (the parent). Then two properties move what is inside:

| Property          | Direction      | Values                                                                             |
|-------------------|----------------|------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|
| `justify-content` | ↔ LEFT-RIGHT   | `flex-start` (left), `center`, `flex-end` (right), `space-between`, `space-around` |
| `align-items`     | ↕ UP-DOWN      | `flex-start` (top), `center`, `flex-end` (bottom)                                  |
| `flex-direction`  | stack children | `row` (next to each other, default), `column` (under each other)                   |

> 💡 Memory trick: **J**ustify = the **J**umping direction (sideways ↔). **A**lign = the other one (↕).  
> ⚠️ With `flex-direction: column` the two SWAP: justify becomes ↕ and align becomes ↔.

```css
.doboz {
  width: 500px;
  height: 300px;
  border: 2px solid black;
  display: flex;
  flex-direction: column;     /* items under each other (title, input, button...) */
  justify-content: center;    /* (because column) middle UP-DOWN */
  align-items: center;        /* (because column) middle LEFT-RIGHT */
  gap: 10px;                  /* space between the items */
}
```

### Way C – padding: push content away from the edges

```css
.doboz { padding: 20px; }        /* everything inside moves 20px away from the border */
.doboz { padding-left: 50px; }   /* only from the left */
```

### Way D – position: absolute (put ONE thing at an EXACT spot, e.g. bottom middle)

> In plain words: the **box** gets `position: relative` ("I'm the frame"). The **thing** gets `position: absolute` ("place me inside the frame by distance from its edges").

```css
.doboz {
  position: relative;          /* THE FRAME. Without this, absolute uses the whole page! */
}

#szam {
  position: absolute;
  bottom: 10px;                /* 10px from the bottom of the box */
  left: 50%;                   /* its LEFT EDGE goes to the middle... */
  transform: translateX(-50%); /* ...then shift it back by half its own width = truly centered */
}

/* other spots: */
/* top right corner:  top: 10px;    right: 10px;  */
/* bottom left:       bottom: 10px; left: 10px;   */
/* top middle:        top: 10px; left: 50%; transform: translateX(-50%); */
```

