## 9. ⭐ Guessing game (Számkitaláló) – with the ruler

> **How the game works in plain words:**  
> 1. The computer secretly picks a random number from 1 to 100 → `titok`  
> 2. You guess → `tipp`  
> 3. If guess \< secret → "Nagyobb" (the secret is bigger). If guess \> secret → "Kisebb". If equal → "Talált!"  
> 4. Count the guesses → `db`  
> 5. Button "Új játék" → pick a new secret and set the counter back to 0

### Random number – the magic line

```js
Math.floor(Math.random() * 100) + 1     // 1 .. 100

// Math.random()        -> 0 .. 0.9999 (random decimal)
// * 100                -> 0 .. 99.99
// Math.floor(...)      -> 0 .. 99   (cut off decimals)
// + 1                  -> 1 .. 100

// general: random between 1 and N:      Math.floor(Math.random() * N) + 1
// between MIN and MAX:                  Math.floor(Math.random() * (MAX - MIN + 1)) + MIN
```

**Full working file – game + ruler + box in the middle**

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="hu">
<head>
<meta charset="UTF-8">
<title>Számkitaláló</title>
<style>
  body {
    font-family: Arial, sans-serif;
    margin: 0;
    height: 100vh;               /* full screen */
    display: flex;               /* center the box... */
    justify-content: center;     /* ...left-right */
    align-items: center;         /* ...up-down */
    background-color: #dfe6f5;
  }
  .doboz {
    position: relative;          /* frame for #mutato */
    width: 560px;
    height: 360px;
    background-color: white;
    border: 2px solid black;
    border-radius: 10px;
    text-align: center;          /* center text/inputs/buttons */
  }
  .vonalzo {
    display: block;
    width: 500px;                /* 500px -> 5px per number */
    height: 60px;
    margin: 15px auto;
    cursor: crosshair;
  }
  #mutato {                      /* number at the BOTTOM MIDDLE of the box */
    position: absolute;
    bottom: 10px;
    left: 50%;
    transform: translateX(-50%);
    font-size: 30px;
    font-weight: bold;
  }
</style>
</head>
<body>

<div class="doboz">
  <h2>Számkitaláló (1-100)</h2>

  <input type="number" id="tipp" min="1" max="100">
  <button onclick="tippel()">Tippel</button>
  <button onclick="indit()">Új játék</button>

  <p id="valasz">Tippelj!</p>
  <p id="szamlalo">Tippek: 0</p>

  <img src="vonalzo.png" class="vonalzo" onmousemove="mozog(event)" onclick="kattint()">

  <div id="mutato">-</div>
</div>

<script>
// ---------- VARIABLES (outside functions, so every function can see them) ----------
let titok;          // the secret number
let db;             // how many guesses so far
let aktualis = 1;   // number under the mouse on the ruler

// ---------- NEW GAME ----------
function indit() {
  titok = Math.floor(Math.random() * 100) + 1;          // 1..100
  db = 0;
  document.getElementById("valasz").innerHTML = "Új játék! Tippelj!";
  document.getElementById("szamlalo").innerHTML = "Tippek: 0";
  document.getElementById("tipp").value = "";
}

// ---------- ONE GUESS ----------
function tippel() {
  let t = Number(document.getElementById("tipp").value);   // read + make it a number

  if (t < 1 || t > 100) {                                   // bad input -> stop
    document.getElementById("valasz").innerHTML = "1 és 100 közötti számot adj meg!";
    return;
  }

  db = db + 1;                                              // count it
  document.getElementById("szamlalo").innerHTML = "Tippek: " + db;

  if (t < titok) {
    document.getElementById("valasz").innerHTML = t + " → Nagyobb!";
  } else if (t > titok) {
    document.getElementById("valasz").innerHTML = t + " → Kisebb!";
  } else {
    document.getElementById("valasz").innerHTML = "Talált! A szám " + titok + " volt. (" + db + " tipp)";
  }
}

// ---------- RULER: mouse moves ----------
function mozog(event) {
  let szelesseg = event.target.clientWidth;                     // ruler width
  aktualis = Math.floor(event.offsetX / szelesseg * 100) + 1;   // 1..100
  if (aktualis > 100) aktualis = 100;
  if (aktualis < 1) aktualis = 1;
  document.getElementById("mutato").innerHTML = aktualis;       // show at bottom middle
}

// ---------- RULER: click = use as guess ----------
function kattint() {
  document.getElementById("tipp").value = aktualis;   // put it into the input
  tippel();                                           // and guess with it
}

// ---------- start the first game when the page opens ----------
indit();
</script>
</body>
</html>
```

### Line by line – what to remember

| Code                                   | Why                                                                                                         |
|----------------------------------------|-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|
| `let titok; let db;` OUTSIDE functions | If you put them inside a function, they are forgotten when it ends, and the other functions can't see them. |
| `Number(...value)`                     | Otherwise "5" is text, and comparisons can act weird.                                                       |
| `return;`                              | Stops the function immediately (bad input → don't count it).                                                |
| `if / else if / else`                  | Exactly ONE of the three answers runs.                                                                      |
| `db = db + 1;` (or `db++`)             | Counter +1.                                                                                                 |
| `kattint()` calls `tippel()`           | A function can call another function, so you don't write the checking twice.                                |
| `indit();` at the end                  | Without it there is no secret number until you press "Új játék".                                            |

